description:
PyArray_ITER_GOTO1D doesn't update coordinates in non contiguous mode, which is used by PyArrayNeighborhoodIterObject to calculate it's own position on PyArrayNeighborhoodIter_Reset, leaving the PyArrayNeighborhoodIterObject pointing to the last position before the call to PyArray_ITER_GOTO1D.

Note that at creation of a new PyArrayNeighborhoodIterObject, if forces a non contiguous mode on the underlying iterator.

### Reproducing code example:

<!-- A short code example that reproduces the problem/missing feature. It should be
self-contained, i.e., possible to run as-is via 'python myproblem.py' -->

```c
//img is a 2D contiguous array (1200x1200)
PyArrayIterObject *iter = (PyArrayIterObject *) PyArray_IterNew((PyObject*) img);
npy_intp bounds[] = {-1,1,-1,1};
PyArrayNeighborhoodIterObject*neigh_iter = (PyArrayNeighborhoodIterObject*) PyArray_NeighborhoodIterNew(
                  iter, bounds, NPY_NEIGHBORHOOD_ITER_ZERO_PADDING ,0);
PyArray_ITER_GOTO1D(iter,1000);
PyArrayNeighborhoodIter_Reset(neigh_iter);
// At this point, iter is pointing to the 1000th item,
// but neigh_iter is still pointing to the 0th entry on iter
```

Backport of #11694.

Fixes #11656, which is a regression after #10564.

Adds tests for pickling datetime64 and timedelta64 scalars. Pickling arrays of these `dtype`s works but pickling scalars fails. 

The problem seems to be in the new code for `gentype_getbuffer`, which creates a PEP 3118 compliant buffer. The old code was:
```C
int gentype_getbuffer(PyObject *self, Py_buffer *view, int flags)
{
    Py_ssize_t len;
    void *buf;
    /* FIXME: XXX: the format is not implemented! -- this needs more work */
    len = gentype_getreadbuf(self, 0, &buf);
    return PyBuffer_FillInfo(view, self, buf, len, 1, flags);
}
```
so now I need to find what is happening in that code that is not happening in the new code.

So far I only found where we override an original exception with a new one. ~Now `memoryview(np.datetime64('2016-01-01'))` raises an exception with the same message as `memoryview(np.array(100, 'M8[D]').~

Edit: python2 - python3 confusion
