Honestly, the only function that truly received a new set of annotations here is `show_config`;
all the other ones were either aliases or re-exports that previously were not marked as such.

I noticed some redundancies in `double random_loggam(double x)` so I made some adjustments to improve performance:
  - moved above the special return-cases to skip unused assignments;
  - since `xp` equals `2.0 * M_PI`, but `log(xp)` is used instead, I suggest to pre-compute that in order to avoid unneeded floating-point operations;
  - shrink the inequality cases, for which block of code is not called anyways;
  - also (don't know if this has any practical utility) I would suggest to split up the initialization of `x2` avoiding the direct computation of `1.0 / (x0 * x0)`, which will cause overflow for large `x0`.

